srow(357, 29, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE SERVANT OF THE LORD" — SCRIPTURE SPEAKS NOT IN MOSES\' DISPRAISE BUT IN HIS PRAISE, FOR SO WE FIND THE FIRST PROPHETS CALLED SERVANTS: "FOR THE LORD GOD DOES NOTHING BUT HE REVEALS HIS COUNSEL TO HIS SERVANTS THE PROPHETS" (Amos 3:7). ({SP_(357, 29, "לא", "בגנותו", "של", "משה", "הכתוב", "מדבר", "אלא")} "not in the dispraise of Moses does Scripture speak but"; {SP_(357, 29, "בנביאים", "הראשונים", "שנקראו", "עבדים")} "the first prophets who were called servants"): THE SERVANT A TITLE — "the servant of the LORD" once in the Torah (the ink), Joshua\'s book\'s name for Moses (Joshua 1:1 and thirteen more — the Prophets\' seats cited never read), Amos 3:7\'s servants the prophets (cited never read); Numbers 12:7\'s "My servant Moses" on the tape (a RUN CITATION). The compile: a status on Moses (servant_of_the_lord — the title given at death). DV34-03. Fresh.')
srow(357, 30, 'MATERIAL', f'"BY THE MOUTH OF THE LORD" — WHEN THE PLACE TAKES THE SOUL OF THE RIGHTEOUS HE TAKES IT GENTLY; A PARABLE: A TRUSTWORTHY MAN IN A CITY WITH WHOM ALL DEPOSITED PLEDGES — WHEN ONE CAME HIMSELF TO CLAIM HIS OWN, HE BROUGHT IT OUT AT ONCE, KNOWING WHERE IT WAS; WHEN ONE SENT BY HIS SON, HIS SERVANT, HIS MESSENGER, HE TURNED THE PLACE UPSIDE DOWN, NOT KNOWING WHERE IT WAS — SO THE SOULS OF THE RIGHTEOUS ARE TAKEN GENTLY AND THE SOULS OF THE WICKED HANDED TO EVIL AND CRUEL ANGELS: "A CRUEL MESSENGER SHALL BE SENT AGAINST HIM" (Proverbs 17:11), "THEIR SOUL DIES IN YOUTH" (Job 36:14). ({SP_(357, 30, "כשהמקום", "נוטל", "נשמתם", "של", "צדיקים", "נוטלה", "מהם")} "when the Place takes the soul of the righteous He takes it from them"; {SP_(357, 30, "לאחד", "נאמן", "שהיה", "בעיר")} "to a trustworthy man who was in a city"; {SP_(357, 30, "מוסרה", "למלאכים", "רעים")} "He hands it to evil angels"): THE DEATH BY THE MOUTH — the soul taken by the Place Himself, gently (the tradition\'s kiss; Onkelos\'s Memra; 305:5\'s angel refused), the trustee\'s PARABLE (E26, mashal — the deposit claimed by its owner against the messenger); the Writings\' seats cited never read. The compile: a DATA note on the manner of the death (no law; the compile\'s "by the mouth of the LORD" the act\'s own phrase, Aaron\'s twin). DV34-03. Fresh.')
srow(357, 31, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE BURIED HIM IN THE VALLEY" — IF "IN THE VALLEY", WHY "IN THE LAND OF MOAB"; IF "IN THE LAND OF MOAB", WHY "IN THE VALLEY"? TO SAY THAT MOSES DIED WITHIN REUBEN\'S INHERITANCE AND WAS BURIED IN THE FIELD OF GAD\'S INHERITANCE. ({SP_(357, 31, "לומר", "שמת", "משה", "בתוך", "נחלתו", "של", "ראובן")} "to say that Moses died within the inheritance of Reuben"; {SP_(357, 31, "ונקבר", "בשדה", "נחלתו", "של", "גד")} "and was buried in the field of the inheritance of Gad"): DIED IN REUBEN\'S, BURIED IN GAD\'S — the two place-phrases read as two places: 355:6\'s and Onkelos 33:21\'s teaching (the great scribe buried in Gad\'s portion) PAID here, the Tosefta\'s four mil the distance (Sotah 4:4 — the testing shelf\'s row); Nebo Reuben\'s (Numbers 32:38 on the tape). The compile: THE POINTER 33:21 -> 34:6 PAID — a DATA row (the grave\'s two tribes) beside the burial act; the readback row at 22b (grade R). DV34-03. Fresh.')
srow(357, 32, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND NO MAN KNOWS HIS GRAVE" — SOME SAY EVEN MOSES DOES NOT KNOW THE PLACE OF HIS GRAVE, FOR "MAN" IS MOSES: "NOW THE MAN MOSES WAS VERY MEEK" (Numbers 12:3). AND ONCE THE HOUSE OF CAESAR SENT TWO DETACHMENTS: GO AND SEE WHERE MOSES\' GRAVE IS — THEY STOOD ABOVE AND SAW IT BELOW, WENT BELOW AND SAW IT ABOVE; THEY DIVIDED, HALF ABOVE AND HALF BELOW — THE UPPER SAW IT BELOW AND THE LOWER SAW IT ABOVE; THEREFORE "NO MAN KNOWS HIS GRAVE". ({SP_(357, 32, "אף", "משה", "אינו", "יודע", "מקום", "קבורתו")} "even Moses does not know the place of his grave"; {SP_(357, 32, "וכבר", "שלחה", "מלכות", "בית", "קיסר", "שני", "סרדיוטות")} "and once the kingdom of the house of Caesar sent two detachments"): THE GRAVE UNKNOWN — "man" read as Moses by Numbers 12:3\'s "the man Moses" (on the tape — a RUN CITATION; E28\'s kin, the word\'s seat elsewhere), Caesar\'s search (Sotah 13b-14a the Talmud\'s seat, OWED). The compile: a status on Moses (grave_unknown — "to this day" the narrator\'s); no law. DV34-03. Fresh.')
srow(357, 33, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND MOSES WAS A HUNDRED AND TWENTY YEARS OLD" — ONE OF FOUR WHO DIED AT A HUNDRED AND TWENTY: MOSES, HILLEL THE ELDER, RABBAN YOCHANAN BEN ZAKKAI AND RABBI AKIVA — MOSES FORTY YEARS IN EGYPT, FORTY IN MIDIAN, FORTY LEADING ISRAEL; HILLEL CAME UP FROM BABYLON AT FORTY, SERVED THE SAGES FORTY, LED ISRAEL FORTY; RABBAN YOCHANAN IN TRADE FORTY, SERVED FORTY, LED FORTY; RABBI AKIVA LEARNED TORAH AT FORTY, SERVED FORTY, LED FORTY. SIX PAIRS WHOSE YEARS WERE EQUAL: REBEKAH AND KOHATH, LEVI AND AMRAM, JOSEPH AND JOSHUA, SAMUEL AND SOLOMON, MOSES AND HILLEL, RABBAN YOCHANAN AND RABBI AKIVA. ({SP_(357, 33, "זה", "אחד", "מארבעה", "שמתו", "בן", "מאה", "ועשרים")} "this is one of four who died at a hundred and twenty"; {SP_(357, 33, "משה", "היה", "במצרים", "ארבעים", "שנה")} "Moses was in Egypt forty years"; {SP_(357, 33, "שש", "זוגות", "ששנותיהם", "שוות")} "six pairs whose years are equal"): THE THREE FORTIES — Moses\' hundred and twenty divided (Egypt, Midian, the leading: Exodus 7:7\'s eighty on the tape, 31:2\'s hundred and twenty the marker\'s — the ink), the four sages\' lives the tradition\'s own (Avot deRabbi Natan the translator\'s parallel), the six pairs (Kohath 133 Exodus 6:18, Amram 137 Exodus 6:20, Joseph 110 Genesis 50:22 — on the tape; Joshua 110 Joshua 24:29, Solomon 1 Kings 11:42 — cited never read). The compile: the age a DATA row (the parser\'s 120 = 31:2\'s, no second marker), the six pairs a DATA row (the tape\'s ages cited: Kohath\'s, Amram\'s, Joseph\'s). DV34-04. Fresh.')
srow(357, 34, 'MATERIAL', f'"HIS EYE WAS NOT DIM" — IT TEACHES THAT THE EYES OF THE DEAD ARE DIM. ({SP_(357, 34, "מלמד", "שעיניהם", "של", "מתים", "כהות")} "it teaches that the eyes of the dead are dim"): THE EYES OF THE DEAD — the exception proves the rule (the dead see dimly — 357:41\'s "the dead see"). The compile: a status on Moses (eye_undimmed); no law. DV34-04. Fresh.')
srow(357, 35, 'MATERIAL', f'"NOR HIS NATURAL FORCE ABATED" — RABBI ELIEZER BEN JACOB: READ NOT "HIS FORCE HAD NOT ABATED" BUT "HIS FORCE HAS NOT ABATED" EVEN NOW: WHOEVER TOUCHES MOSES\' FLESH, THE FRESHNESS WELLS UP THIS WAY AND THAT. ({SP_(357, 35, "כל", "הנוגע", "בבשרו", "של", "משה", "לחה", "פורחת")} "whoever touches the flesh of Moses, the freshness wells"): THE FRESHNESS EVEN NOW — the "do not read" (the tense turned present; no code in MIDDOT\'s lists, named by its row): the body incorrupt — Onkelos\'s splendor of the face unchanged (34:7\'s rendering), the grave no man knows. The compile: a status on Moses (force_unabated); no law. DV34-04. Fresh.')
srow(357, 36, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL WEPT FOR MOSES" — THAT IS ONE; "AND THE DAYS WERE ENDED" — THAT IS TWO; "THE WEEPING OF THE MOURNING FOR MOSES" — THAT IS THREE. ({SP_(357, 36, "את", "משה", "הרי", "אחד")} "for Moses — that is one"; {SP_(357, 36, "בכי", "אבל", "משה", "הרי", "שלשה")} "the weeping of the mourning for Moses — that is three"): THE THREE COUNTED — the verse\'s three phrases three days (the translator) or three mournings; the compile: a DATA row beside the thirty days\' duration (the counter\'s matter at 22b). DV34-04. Fresh.')
srow(357, 37, 'MATERIAL', f'"THIRTY DAYS" — WHAT ARE THESE FOR? IT TEACHES THAT THEY WEPT FOR HIM THIRTY DAYS BEFORE THE DEATH. AND WHENCE THAT THE DAYS OF A NAZIRITE ARE THIRTY? IT IS SAID HERE "DAYS" AND IT IS SAID THERE "THE DAYS" (Numbers 6:4): AS THE DAYS HERE ARE THIRTY, SO THE DAYS THERE ARE THIRTY. ({SP_(357, 37, "שבכו", "אותו", "קדם", "למיתה", "שלשים", "יום")} "that they wept for him before the death thirty days"; {SP_(357, 37, "ומנין", "לימי", "נזירות", "שהם", "שלשים", "יום")} "and whence that the days of naziriteship are thirty days"): THE NAZIRITE\'S THIRTY BY THE VERBAL ANALOGY — "days" (34:8) and "the days" (Numbers 6:4): I2, the Sifrei\'s own, the source of Nazir 1:3\'s thirty (the Mishnah\'s row — the compile\'s case; the nazirite\'s runner at Numbers 6 on the tape by CALL: its unspecified term a PARAMETER the answer sheet fills from this verse — the code/data law\'s own exhibit: the number lives in Deuteronomy 34:8, the rule in Numbers 6); the thirty before the death (the weeping foreknown — 31:14\'s "your days approach"). The compile: THE PARAMETER the_nazirite_term = 30 sourced here (22b: the nazirite\'s runner reads it by CALL — the last chapter supplies a datum to the sixth of Numbers), the duration on the counter 22b\'s decision. DV34-04. Fresh.')
srow(357, 38, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND JOSHUA THE SON OF NUN WAS FULL OF THE SPIRIT OF WISDOM" — WHY? "FOR MOSES HAD LAID HIS HANDS UPON HIM". ({SP_(357, 38, "מפני", "מה")} "why"; {SP_(357, 38, "כי", "סמך", "משה", "את", "ידיו", "עליו")} "for Moses laid his hands upon him"): THE CAUSE IN THE VERSE — the wisdom from the hands (Numbers 27:18-23 on the tape — the commission\'s act, its receipt here). The compile: the receipt of the laying on of hands (invested_office on Joshua unmoved); the spirit a status (spirit_of_wisdom). DV34-05. Fresh.')
srow(357, 39, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE CHILDREN OF ISRAEL HEARKENED TO HIM" — YOU HAVE NO GREATER OBEDIENCE THAN THIS; "AND DID AS THE LORD COMMANDED MOSES" — BUT HIS AWE WAS NOT YET UPON THEM, AS IT IS SAID "ON THAT DAY THE LORD MAGNIFIED JOSHUA" (Joshua 4:14) — AT THAT HOUR HIS AWE WAS PUT UPON THEM. ({SP_(357, 39, "אין", "לך", "משמע", "גדול", "מזה")} "you have no obedience greater than this"; {SP_(357, 39, "ועדין", "לא", "נתן", "מוראו", "עליהם")} "but his awe was not yet put upon them"): THE OBEDIENCE AND THE AWE — the hearkening complete at Moses\' death, the awe at the Jordan (Joshua 4:14 the Prophets\' seat cited never read — the honor of 31:7\'s charge "in the sight of all Israel"); "as the LORD commanded Moses" the register\'s receipt (34:9). The compile: a status on Israel (hearkened_to_joshua), the awe a pointer ahead (the Prophets\' tape). DV34-05. Fresh.')
srow(357, 40, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THERE HAS NOT ARISEN A PROPHET SINCE IN ISRAEL LIKE MOSES" — IN ISRAEL NONE AROSE, BUT AMONG THE NATIONS ONE AROSE: BALAAM THE SON OF BEOR. BUT THERE IS A DIFFERENCE: MOSES DID NOT KNOW WHO SPOKE WITH HIM, BALAAM KNEW ("WHO HEARS THE WORDS OF GOD" Numbers 24:16); MOSES DID NOT KNOW WHEN HE WOULD SPEAK UNTIL HE SPOKE, BALAAM KNEW ("WHO KNOWS THE KNOWLEDGE OF THE MOST HIGH"); MOSES WAS SPOKEN WITH ONLY STANDING ("BUT YOU, STAND HERE BY ME" 5:28), BALAAM FALLEN ("FALLEN DOWN, YET WITH OPENED EYES" Numbers 24:4). A PARABLE: THE KING\'S COOK KNOWS WHAT THE KING\'S TABLE COSTS. ({SP_(357, 40, "בישראל", "לא", "קם")} "in Israel none arose"; {SP_(357, 40, "אבל", "באמות", "העולם", "קם")} "but among the nations of the world one arose"; {SP_(357, 40, "זה", "בלעם", "בן", "בעור")} "this is Balaam the son of Beor"; {SP_(357, 40, "לטבחו", "של", "מלך")} "to the cook of a king"): BALAAM THE NATIONS\' PROPHET — "in Israel" read as the limit (E28\'s kin), the three differences from Numbers 24:4 and 24:16 (on the tape — the oracles\' runner, RUN CITATIONS) and 5:28\'s "stand here by Me" (the row\'s own seat, read at chapter 5 — the export\'s 5:28 = the DB\'s 5:31; REREAD here), the king\'s cook the PARABLE (E26). The compile: prophet_unequalled\'s status bounded to Israel (a DATA row: the nations\' Balaam — the oracles\' entries cited). DV34-06. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 5\'s reading — 5:28).')
srow(357, 41, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHOM THE LORD KNEW FACE TO FACE" — WHY IS IT SAID? BECAUSE "SHOW ME, I PRAY, YOUR GLORY" (Exodus 33:18) — HE SAID TO HIM: IN THIS WORLD YOU DO NOT SEE, WHICH IS LIKENED TO THE FACE ("YOU CANNOT SEE MY FACE" Exodus 33:20), BUT YOU SEE IN THE WORLD TO COME, WHICH IS LIKENED TO THE BACK ("I WILL TAKE AWAY MY HAND AND YOU SHALL SEE MY BACK" Exodus 33:23). WHEN DID HE SHOW HIM? NEAR THE DEATH — YOU LEARN THAT THE DEAD SEE. ({SP_(357, 41, "בעולם", "הזה", "אי", "אתה", "רואה")} "in this world you do not see"; {SP_(357, 41, "אבל", "אתה", "רואה", "בעולם", "הבא")} "but you see in the world to come"; {SP_(357, 41, "הא", "למדת", "שהמתים", "רואים")} "you learn that the dead see"): THE FACE AT DEATH — Exodus 33:18-23 on the tape (the cleft of the rock — RUN CITATIONS: the face refused, the back shown), "face to face" (34:10, Exodus 33:11) read as the sight granted at the death (this world the face-likened, the world to come the back-likened — the two worlds of 32:4\'s and 33:6\'s rows); "the dead see" with 357:34\'s dim eyes. The compile: a DATA note beside prophet_unequalled; the world to come\'s doctrine cited (Sanhedrin 10:1 the compile\'s case at the blessing). DV34-06. Fresh.')
srow(357, 42, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN ALL THE SIGNS AND THE WONDERS WHICH THE LORD SENT HIM TO DO IN THE LAND OF EGYPT, TO PHARAOH AND TO ALL HIS SERVANTS AND TO ALL HIS LAND" — TO EGYPT FOR ITSELF, TO PHARAOH FOR HIMSELF, TO HIS SERVANTS FOR THEMSELVES. ({SP_(357, 42, "למצרים", "בפני", "עצמה")} "to Egypt for itself"; {SP_(357, 42, "לפרעה", "בפני", "עצמו")} "to Pharaoh for himself"; {SP_(357, 42, "ולעבדיו", "בפני", "עצמם")} "and to his servants for themselves"): THE THREE ADDRESSEES — the verse\'s three "to"s three plagues\' targets (the plagues on Egypt, on Pharaoh, on his servants — Exodus 7-12 on the tape, RUN CITATIONS; 29:1\'s line the twin). The compile: a DATA row (the signs\' three objects). DV34-06. Fresh.')
srow(357, 43, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND IN ALL THE MIGHTY HAND" — THIS IS THE PLAGUE OF THE FIRSTBORN; "AND IN ALL THE GREAT TERROR" — THIS IS THE SPLITTING OF THE SEA OF REEDS. ({SP_(357, 43, "זו", "מכת", "בכורות")} "this is the plague of the firstborn"; {SP_(357, 43, "זו", "קריעת", "ים", "סוף")} "this is the splitting of the sea of Reeds"): THE HAND AND THE TERROR NAMED — the firstborn\'s plague (Exodus 12:29 on the tape) and the sea (Exodus 14:21 on the tape — Exodus 14:31\'s "the great hand" the ink\'s twin): RUN CITATIONS; the two the Torah\'s last verse points back to (34:12\'s words at this row — the seat rule by row keeps it at 34:11, its citing row before). The compile: a DATA row (the last verse\'s referents). DV34-06. Fresh.')
srow(357, 44, 'MATERIAL', f'RABBI ELAZAR: "IN ALL THE SIGNS AND THE WONDERS" — AND WHENCE ALSO BEFORE MOUNT SINAI? "AND IN ALL THE MIGHTY HAND". AND WHENCE ALSO IN THE WILDERNESS? "AND IN ALL THE GREAT TERROR". AND WHENCE ALSO THE BREAKING OF THE TABLETS? IT IS SAID THERE "AND I BROKE THEM BEFORE YOUR EYES" (9:17), AND HERE IT SAYS "WHICH MOSES WROUGHT IN THE SIGHT OF ALL ISRAEL". ({SP_(357, 44, "ומנין", "אף", "לפני", "הר", "סיני")} "and whence also before Mount Sinai"; {SP_(357, 44, "ומנין", "אף", "בשבור", "הלוחות")} "and whence also at the breaking of the tablets"; {SP_(357, 44, "וכאן", "הוא", "אומר", "אשר", "עשה", "משה", "לעיני")} "and here it says: which Moses did in the sight of"): THE EXPORT\'S LAST ROW — the Sifrei\'s last teaching on the Torah\'s last words: the signs at Sinai, in the wilderness and THE TABLETS BROKEN "before your eyes" (9:17 — the row\'s own seat, read at chapter 9 and REREAD here; the verbal analogy "before your eyes" / "in the sight of" — I2 by sense, the ink sharing no token) — the breaking a sign Moses wrought, the tradition\'s approval of it (Shabbat 87a\'s "may your strength be firm" the Talmud\'s seat, OWED); the calf\'s tablets on the tape (Exodus 32:19 — a RUN CITATION). The compile: a DATA row (the last verse\'s referents widened: Sinai, the wilderness, the tablets); the book\'s and the shelf\'s edge — nothing after this row (the ink asserts the export ends). DV34-06. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 9\'s reading — 9:17).')
